    "created_at": "2016-08-23T18:41:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-23T18:42:22Z",
    "body": "I don't see why it is necessary to create a new SubPath interface. We could just have CanvasPath.getSubPaths() that returns an array of Path2D objects.  And the other suggested APIs could all hang off of the CanvasPath interface IMHO. I see no problem in evaluatin length on a path composed of many sub-paths\n\nI really think this proposal ought to be split into 3 simple orthogonal proposals (assuming we don't need SubPath):\n- CanvasPath.getSubPaths(), returning an array of Path2Ds\n- CanvasPath.length + pointAt\n- CanvasPath.getBoundingRect()\n\nThis would allow each sub feature's merit and design to be discussed and tweaked independently of each other in neat little threads.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
